# Normalize line endings for every text file.
#
# The index already stores LF (`git ls-files --eol` reports `i/lf`), but Windows
# checkouts get CRLF in the working tree. Prettier is configured with
# `endOfLine: "lf"`, so `prettier --check` reports false positives on Windows for
# files that are byte-correct in git — which made `format:check` unreliable
# locally and hid real formatting drift behind noise.
#
# `eol=lf` makes the working tree match the index on every platform, so a local
# `format:check` result means the same thing as CI's.
#
# NOTE: taking effect on an existing clone requires a one-off
# `git add --renormalize .` followed by a checkout. Since the index is already
# LF, that should produce no content diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be normalized.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
